{
 "id": "2026-10-26-binary-search-thirty",
 "topic": "binary search: a billion numbers need only 30 guesses (log2)",
 "subject": "computing",
 "hook_type": "wrong-answer reveal",
 "caption": "Each guess halves the remaining numbers, so n numbers need about log2(n) guesses. A billion is between 2^29 and 2^30, so thirty guesses always suffice and twenty-nine cannot. A thousand times more data adds only about ten guesses.\n\nSave this for your next algorithms interview.\n\n#computerscience #algorithms #binarysearch #programming #math #logarithm #coding #stem #softwareengineering",
 "cover_at": 1.0,
 "hook": "Guess a number from 1 to a billion. How many tries?",
 "sub": "Thirty is enough, every time.",
 "beats": [
  {
   "text": "I'm thinking of a whole number from 1 to 1,000,000,000. After each guess, I only say higher or lower.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "rg",
     "tex": "1\\;\\ldots\\;1{,}000{,}000{,}000",
     "size": 60,
     "at": [
      0,
      4.0
     ]
    },
    {
     "make": "shape",
     "name": "r1",
     "kind": "rect",
     "w": 6.4,
     "h": 0.6,
     "center": [
      0,
      2.6
     ],
     "color": "blue",
     "fill": 0.5
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Guess the middle. Whatever I answer, half of the numbers are gone.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "shape",
     "name": "r2",
     "kind": "rect",
     "w": 3.2,
     "h": 0.6,
     "center": [
      -1.6,
      1.7
     ],
     "color": "teal",
     "fill": 0.5
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Again: a quarter left. Again: an eighth. Every guess halves what remains.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "shape",
     "name": "r3",
     "kind": "rect",
     "w": 1.6,
     "h": 0.6,
     "center": [
      -2.4,
      0.8
     ],
     "color": "yellow",
     "fill": 0.5
    },
    {
     "make": "shape",
     "name": "r4",
     "kind": "rect",
     "w": 0.8,
     "h": 0.6,
     "center": [
      -2.8,
      -0.1
     ],
     "color": "green",
     "fill": 0.5
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "After $k$ guesses, about $10^9 / 2^k$ numbers remain. We're done when that gets down to one.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "eq",
     "tex": [
      "\\frac{10^9}{2^k}",
      "\\approx",
      "1"
     ],
     "size": 96,
     "at": [
      0,
      -1.6
     ],
     "colors": {
      "0": "yellow"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "do": [
    {
     "clear": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Let's plot the guesses needed, $k$, against the size of the range, $n$.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "axes",
     "name": "ax",
     "x": [
      0,
      1024,
      256
     ],
     "y": [
      0,
      10,
      2
     ],
     "size": [
      7.0,
      5.0
     ],
     "at": [
      0,
      0.8
     ],
     "labels": [
      "n",
      "k"
     ]
    },
    {
     "make": "graph",
     "name": "g",
     "on": "ax",
     "fn": "ln(x)/ln(2)",
     "x": [
      1,
      1024
     ],
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "make": "tracker",
     "name": "t",
     "value": 1
    },
    {
     "make": "dot",
     "name": "p",
     "follow": "g",
     "x": "t",
     "color": "yellow"
    },
    {
     "make": "readout",
     "name": "ro",
     "tracker": "t",
     "fn": "ln(x)/ln(2)",
     "label": "\\log_2 n =",
     "decimals": 1,
     "at": [
      0,
      4.9
     ],
     "color": "yellow"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Double the range and you add just one guess. Watch it climb, then flatten.",
   "do": [
    {
     "sfx": "whoosh"
    },
    {
     "slide": "t",
     "to": 1024,
     "time": 3.5
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "do": [
    {
     "clear": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "A billion sits between $2^{29}$ and $2^{30}$. Twenty-nine guesses can't separate every number. Thirty can.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "a1",
     "tex": [
      "2^{29}",
      "=",
      "536{,}870{,}912",
      "<",
      "10^9"
     ],
     "size": 52,
     "at": [
      0,
      3.6
     ],
     "colors": {
      "2": "red"
     }
    },
    {
     "sfx": "riser"
    },
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "a2",
     "tex": [
      "2^{30}",
      "=",
      "1{,}073{,}741{,}824",
      ">",
      "10^9"
     ],
     "size": 52,
     "next_to": "a1",
     "buff": 0.7,
     "colors": {
      "2": "green"
     }
    },
    {
     "sfx": "ding"
    },
    {
     "make": "box",
     "name": "bx",
     "around": "a2",
     "color": "green"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "So thirty guesses always find it. A thousand times more numbers costs only about ten more.",
   "do": [
    {
     "hide": "bx"
    },
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "fin",
     "tex": [
      "30",
      "\\text{ guesses for }",
      "10^9"
     ],
     "size": 56,
     "at": [
      0,
      0.6
     ],
     "colors": {
      "0": "yellow"
     }
    },
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "fin2",
     "tex": [
      "40",
      "\\text{ guesses for }",
      "10^{12}"
     ],
     "size": 56,
     "next_to": "fin",
     "buff": 0.5,
     "colors": {
      "0": "green"
     }
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
 "outro": "Follow for more ideas like this.",
 "approved": true
}